 "note": {
  "status": "draft",
  "text": "Types of urban problems in Cameroon:\n• environmental: floods (Douala, Yaoundé's Mfoundi valley), rubbish, air pollution, landslides on hills (Bafoussam, Limbe);\n• social: housing shortage, crime, drug abuse, street children, overcrowded schools and hospitals;\n• economic: unemployment, high cost of living, informal sector;\n• infrastructure: traffic jams, bad roads, water and electricity shortages.\nCauses: rapid population growth, poor planning, poverty, building in risky zones, poor waste disposal.\nConsequences: diseases, loss of life and property in floods and landslides, insecurity, stress.\nPractical solutions: respect town plans and do not build in swamps or on steep slopes; collect and recycle waste; plant trees; build drains; improve public transport; create jobs; community clean-ups.",
  "checks": []
 },
 "worked_example": {
  "status": "draft",
  "vars": {},
  "problem": "Why are landslides a risk on the hills of some Cameroonian towns, and what can be done?",
  "steps": [
   "Houses are built on steep slopes, and trees are cut, so heavy rain loosens the soil.",
   "Solutions: do not build on steep slopes, plant trees and build drains."
  ],
  "answer": "Building on steep slopes and cutting trees; plant trees, build drains and avoid steep slopes.",
  "checks": []
 },
